  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "5fbk36v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Gregor Mendel is recognized as the Father of Genetics for his pioneering work on pea plants (Pisum sativum).",
        "Human somatic cells contain 23 pairs of chromosomes, consisting of 22 pairs of autosomes and 1 pair of sex chromosomes.",
        "DNA carries genetic information in a double-helix structure containing Adenine, Thymine, Guanine, and Cytosine.",
        "Mendel proposed three fundamental principles: Law of Dominance, Law of Segregation, and Law of Independent Assortment.",
        "Gene mutations can be point mutations or frameshift mutations, leading to genetic disorders like Sickle Cell Anemia."
      ],
      "id": "s0zru0c"
    },
